A||||4||aubicon||5 point harnesses||||1||
Z||000000||aubicon||09-24-2001||10:48 PM||||has anyone installed 5 point harnesses in their fiero. i want to use y-type harnesses and i figured that i could just bolt them straight through the rear windowsill. but im not sure if that will be strong enough. i dont want to do to much frame modification if i can avoid it. any idias.||||reg||1
Z||000001||OcalaFiero||09-25-2001||09:25 AM||||I'm not sure, but in most cases racing harnesses aren't street legal. If you're going to race it, or just put them in anyway, make sure you do it right. The Harnesses need to be mounted correctly, or you'll be eating steering wheel. The lap belts need to be securely mounted to the floor pan, you can probably get away with the stock locations. The shoulder harness needs to be mounted to either a frame member or a bar that runs across the area behind the seat, just below shoulder level. You can't just mount them to the seats or window frame, as these places just arent strong enough. Hope this helps.<P>   <P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR>'86 2M4<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallsigpic_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-25-2001||08:07 PM||||All harness makers have specific requirements for installation of their belt systems. Failing to follow these specifications can have fatal results. Don't take my word for it. Read the reports published by NASCAR and Simpson regarding the Ernhart wreck. <P>I strongly recomend you contact the maker of your planed belts before purchase to obtain the mounting requirements. Do not assume the seat or any of the OE harness anchorage is suitable for use with the new harness systems. Most race harness systems cannot be used correctly with many factory seats. The seat back inteferes with the shoulder harness sections. The seat bottom requires major lateration to work with an anti sub strap.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||09-26-2001||10:17 AM||||The integral headrest on the stock Fiero seats is a real problem when using a harness.  I installed a seat from an Acura Integra (not recommended!) as an interim. The lap belt is mounted to the stock points and the shoulder belts have individual points. I used two pieces of 4x4" 3/16 flat bar bolted to the back of the firewall on either side of the hinge mount. It's worth while to be overly cautious with this stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000004||85 gt fiero||09-26-2001||04:42 PM||||i have 4 point harneses on my rally car fiero the two that go around your shoulder conect to the back firewall the guy welded steel plates from the roll cage and there connected to little hooks, and the waist one is mounted to the skid plates on the bottom, to little brackets.  Since you dont have a rool cage you could take out some of the firewall insalation and mount the hooks there but you might end up reinforcing it some how.  Good Luck   Randy||||reg||1
